    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="A and C are fixed on the circle. Drag B along the circle: angle ABC doesn't change!\n\nAll inscribed angles that intercept the same arc are congruent, and each is half of the central angle AOC.\n\nNow move A and C so that AC is a diameter. The angle becomes exactly 90°." DecimalsToShow="2" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="105.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
